How We Connect — Communication Preferences & Rules
:::

:::shape id=s3_col1_bg x=80 y=140 w=445 h=510 kind=rect fill=#1E293B borderRadius=8
:::

:::text id=s3_col1_txt x=100 y=160 w=405 h=470 preset=body align=left color=#F8FAFC
:::icon[name="message-square" color="#06B6D4"]:::
**Preferred Channels & Rules**

• **Slack/Teams** (Chat): Quick info exchange.
• **Face-to-Face or Call**: Complex/nuanced topics.
• **Email**: Official decisions or external comms.

**Boundaries & Rules:**
• **Context upfront**: Provide context upfront unless already established.
• **One at a time**: Handle only one live call or conversation at a time.
:::

:::shape id=s3_col2_bg x=564 y=140 w=445 h=510 kind=rect fill=#1E293B borderRadius=8
:::

:::text id=s3_col2_txt x=584 y=160 w=405 h=470 preset=body align=left color=#F8FAFC
:::icon[name="list-checks" color="#06B6D4"]:::
**Standard 3-Step Format**

When bringing up questions or discussions, use this structure:

**1. Context (facts only)**
Provide the factual background clearly.

**2. Problem definition**
Define the exact challenge or issue.

**3. Proposed solutions**
Share potential options or recommendations (if any).
:::